     4	// Air cells (cell_meta.w = CELL_AIR after cell_classify: no fluid, center in-box, not inside a
     5	// solid) are flood-filled from the OPEN boundary: the topmost in-box cell layer is the
     6	// atmosphere (the box's side/bottom faces are sealed walls — air sealed against them is still
     7	// enclosed). The flood runs a scene-derived number of ping-pong relaxation sweeps (the grid
     8	// Manhattan diameter — `flood_sweeps_for` in mod.rs; labels in the pressure ping-pong buffers,
     9	// which cell_classify zeroed and pocket_mark re-zeroes) propagating the OUTSIDE label one
    10	// 6-neighbor step per sweep — uniform control flow, deterministic (read old / write new, never
    11	// racy in-place). The budget MUST cover the longest open-air path or genuinely-open air (e.g.
    12	// the deep V60 cup under its cone) is misread as one enclosed pocket and the bubble crushes the
    13	// standing water. Air cells still unlabeled afterwards are ENCLOSED: the
    14	// pocket. Single-pocket case (the pour cavity) per the plan: ALL enclosed air shares ONE
    15	// bubble — multi-pocket generalization is deferred scope.
    16	//
    17	// ================================ BUBBLE REPRESENTATION (KTD-6, pinned) =======================
    18	// ONE explicit Lagrange-multiplier scalar λ_b (bubble[0]); its value IS the pocket pressure.
    19	// Pocket cells are inserted into the SAME operator family as fluid rows: pocket_mark gives
    20	// them fill weight f = 1 and rhs = (0 − D v)/dt (no density relief — air), so
    21	//   * the COLUMN coupling is automatic: fluid rows and the projection gather pocket pressure
    22	//     through the one G = −Dᵀ (the pocket pressure acts on exactly the pocket-boundary faces
    23	//     — interior pocket nodes are massless, M̃⁻¹ = 0, and contribute nothing);
    24	//   * the ROW is the aggregate volume constraint Σ_{c∈pocket}(D u⁺)_c = 0 — the row sum of
    25	//     the per-cell rows, solved EXACTLY for the single unknown each relaxation step:
    26	//         λ_b ← λ_b + (Σ rhs_c − Σ (A p̃)_c) / (1ᵀ_pocket·A·1_pocket),
    27	//     where p̃ carries λ_b in the pocket slots and the denominator is the full aggregated
    28	//     quadratic form (cross terms between pocket cells included — computed as Σ(A·1_pocket)_c).
    29	// IDENTICAL REPRESENTATION AT BOTH LEVELS (the named failure is a coarse-only row the fine
    30	// sweeps relax away — and its mirror image): a bubble_fine step precedes EVERY fine Jacobi
    31	// sweep and jacobi_fine pins pocket slots to λ_b (Dirichlet copy of the multiplier); the
    32	// coarse error equation carries the bubble correction δλ_b (bubble[1]) the same way —
    33	// bubble_coarse precedes every coarse sweep, jacobi_coarse pins all-pocket coarse cells to
    34	// δλ_b, and prolong_add adds δλ_b (a scalar — its prolongation is exact) to the fine pocket
    35	// slots; the next bubble_fine folds λ_b ← λ_b + δλ_b before re-solving. p₀ = 0 doctrine:
    36	// pocket_mark zeroes λ_b and δλ_b every frame (no warm start). When the pocket is OPEN
    37	// (pre-enclosure — e.g. the jet annulus connects the cavity to outside air) there are no
    38	// pocket cells, the aggregated diagonal is 0, and λ_b is pinned inactive (p = 0 air).
    39	//
    40	// Tint discipline: bubble_fine/bubble_coarse run as ONE workgroup with a uniform trip count
    41	// (now over the COMPACTED pocket list, not all cells — U8 R9 fix) and predicated bodies, so
    42	// every workgroupBarrier() is in uniform control flow. All other passes use guard returns with
    43	// no barriers. Over-dispatch + early-out only (R8). Storage buffers per entry point ≤ 7 (see
    44	// MAX_STORAGE_BUFFERS_PER_ENTRY_POINT in mod.rs).
    45	
    46	// --- bindings (continue the global table; 17 is the bubble state) -----------------------------
    47	// bubble[0] = λ_b (fine-level pocket pressure), bubble[1] = δλ_b (coarse correction).
    48	@group(0) @binding(17) var<storage, read_write> bubble: array<f32>;
    49	
    50	// U8 R9 fix: COMPACTED pocket-cell lists (the parallel-reduction approach). Element 0 is an
    51	// atomic append counter, elements [1, 1+count) are the flat cell indices labelled CELL_POCKET
    52	// this frame. flood_init resets both counters; pocket_mark appends the fine pockets and
    53	// coarse_cell_setup appends the coarse pockets. The bubble row solves then iterate the few
    54	// hundred listed cells instead of strided-scanning all ~76k cells per dispatch (the same sums
    55	// over the SAME cells — only the iteration set is compacted, λ_b is unchanged).
    56	@group(0) @binding(26) var<storage, read_write> pocket_f: array<atomic<u32>>;
    57	@group(0) @binding(27) var<storage, read_write> pocket_c: array<atomic<u32>>;
    58	
    59	// cell_meta.w / cmeta.w categories (CELL_AIR is only ever set on fine cells).
    60	const CELL_AIR: f32 = 1.0;
    61	const CELL_POCKET: f32 = 2.0;
    62	// Label values in the flood ping-pong (pressure slots reused before the solve zeroes them).
    63	const FLOOD_OUTSIDE: f32 = 1.0;
    64	
    65	// Minimum resolved-bubble size, in FINE cells. The constant-volume bubble constraint models a
    66	// RESOLVED incompressible air cavity (the pour crater). A pocket of only a handful of cells is
    67	// sub-resolution air: a 3-node (2-cell) B-spline support cannot represent a bubble narrower than
    68	// ~2 cells per axis, so its "incompressibility" is a discretization artifact, not physics — real
    69	// entrained microbubbles are compressible and vent/dissolve. Such a pocket must be RELEASED to
    70	// p = 0 (open air), not pinned to a huge λ. Without this, the V60 cone's draining film
    71	// geometrically isolates 1–7 air cells the 6-neighbor flood cannot reach; the single global
    72	// bubble then assigns them λ ≈ 1e3–1e4, ejecting the standing cup water at the speed cap for
    73	// 100+ frames (the residual WaterOnly artifact after the flood-budget / wall-band fixes). One
    74	// 2×2×2 cell block (8) is the threshold: the legitimate pour cavity is hundreds of cells (the
    75	// cavity gate's enclosed slab is 288), so the band is enormous — this can never gate a real
    76	// cavity. Both levels gate on this one authoritative FINE count (bubble_coarse reads pocket_f[0]
    77	// too), so the coarse correction releases on exactly the same criterion as the fine solve.
    78	const MIN_POCKET_FINE_CELLS: u32 = 8u;
    79	
    80	// =================================== flood_init ================================================
    81	// Seed the OUTSIDE label: air cells in the topmost in-box layer (the open atmosphere face), AND
    82	// every air cell WITHIN ONE CELL OF AN SDF WALL. The wall-adjacent seed is what makes the pocket
    83	// machinery correct in deep SDF geometry like the V60 cup: a 6-neighbor flood cannot squeeze the
    84	// OUTSIDE label down through the ~1-cell-wide cone apex hole (radius 0.42 ≈ 1.3 cells at the web
    85	// h = 0.32) to reach the cup air below, so the whole cup/cone air column was misread as one
    86	// enclosed POCKET and the bubble constraint (λ ≈ −3000) crushed the standing water into the
    87	// floor corner — the reported WaterOnly collapse. A sub-resolution void touching an SDF wall is
    88	// never genuinely trapped gas at this resolution: it is open (fluid settles into the bottom-of-
    89	// column gap; air vents through the apex/wall gap), pressure p = 0. This narrows the bubble to
    90	// air actually sealed away from any wall — the transient pour cavity the machinery exists for
    91	// (the cavity gate scene is a plain box, no SDF walls, so it is byte-unchanged: the extra seed
    92	// only fires when num_solids > 0 AND a wall is within a cell).
    93	@compute @workgroup_size(256)
    94	fn flood_init(@builtin(global_invocation_id) gid: vec3<u32>) {
    95	    let c = gid.x;
    96	    if (c == 0u) {
    97	        bubble[2] = 0.0; // pocket-present flag, raised by pocket_mark this frame
    98	        atomicStore(&pocket_f[0], 0u); // reset the compacted pocket-list counters this frame
    99	        atomicStore(&pocket_c[0], 0u);
   100	    }
   101	    if (c >= num_fine_cells()) {
   102	        return;
   103	    }
   104	    var label = 0.0;
   105	    if (cell_meta[c].w == CELL_AIR) {
   106	        let h = params.grid_origin.w;
   107	        let cc = vec3<f32>(cell_coords(c));
   108	        let center = params.grid_origin.xyz + (cc + vec3<f32>(0.5)) * h;
   109	        if (center.y + h > params.box_max.y) {
   110	            label = FLOOD_OUTSIDE; // the cell above is out of the box: open face
   111	        } else if (params.num_solids > 0u
   112	            && solid_union(center, PHASE_WATER).dist < FLOOD_WALL_BAND * h) {
   113	            // Any air cell within FLOOD_WALL_BAND cells of an SDF wall is OPEN, not trapped gas:
   114	            // a sub-resolution void at a wall (the bottom-of-column floor gap), OR an air cell in
   115	            // a narrow SDF channel the 6-neighbor flood cannot squeeze the label through (the V60
   116	            // cone apex hole, radius 0.42 ≈ 1.3 cells — a center-of-apex air cell sits ~0.42 from
   117	            // the wall, just OUTSIDE the projector's 1-cell band, so the flood seed uses a wider
   118	            // 2-cell band to keep the apex conductive and connect the cup/cone air to the open
   119	            // top). Without this the filled cup seals the cone air into one enclosed pocket and
   120	            // the bubble crushes the pool.
   121	            label = FLOOD_OUTSIDE;
   122	        }
   123	    }
   124	    pf_src[c] = label;
   125	}
   126	
   127	// =================================== flood_sweep ===============================================
   128	// One 6-neighbor propagation step, ping-pong (read 11, write 12). Non-air cells keep label 0
   129	// (fluid blocks propagation), so reading a neighbor's label needs no category check.
   130	@compute @workgroup_size(256)
   131	fn flood_sweep(@builtin(global_invocation_id) gid: vec3<u32>) {
   132	    let c = gid.x;
   133	    if (c >= num_fine_cells()) {
   134	        return;
   135	    }
   136	    var label = 0.0;
   137	    if (cell_meta[c].w == CELL_AIR) {
   138	        label = pf_src[c];
   139	        if (label < 0.5) {
   140	            let cc = vec3<i32>(cell_coords(c));
   141	            for (var a = 0; a < 3; a = a + 1) {
   142	                for (var s = -1; s <= 1; s = s + 2) {
   143	                    var n = cc;
   144	                    n[a] = n[a] + s;
   145	                    if (cell_in_range(n) && pf_src[cell_index(n)] > 0.5) {
   146	                        label = FLOOD_OUTSIDE;
   147	                    }
   148	                }
   149	            }
   150	        }
   151	    }
   152	    pf_dst[c] = label;
   153	}
   154	
   155	// =================================== pocket_mark ===============================================
   156	// Enclosed air (still unlabeled) becomes the pocket: fill weight 1, rhs = (0 − D v)/dt — a
   157	// constraint row of the one family (header: BUBBLE REPRESENTATION). Re-zeroes the pressure
   158	// ping-pong the flood borrowed and resets the bubble scalars (p₀ = 0, fresh λ each frame).
   159	@compute @workgroup_size(256)
   160	fn pocket_mark(@builtin(global_invocation_id) gid: vec3<u32>) {
   161	    let c = gid.x;
   162	    if (c >= num_fine_cells()) {
   163	        return;
   164	    }
   165	    if (c == 0u) {
   166	        bubble[0] = 0.0;
   167	        bubble[1] = 0.0;
   168	    }
   169	    let label = pf_src[c];
   170	    pf_src[c] = 0.0;
   171	    pf_dst[c] = 0.0;
   172	    let cm = cell_meta[c];
   173	    let cc = vec3<i32>(cell_coords(c));
   174	
   175	    // Density relief, UNDER-density half (the deferred-to-U4 suction; over-density half in
   176	    // cell_classify): an INTERIOR cell below rest density demands inflow at the same relief
   177	    // rate, re-compacting rarefied regions (a jet tears a sub-cell void channel whose cells
   178	    // still read f = 1; their div = 0 rows then forbid the refilling inflow and the channel
   179	    // stands frozen forever — observed). Air-ADJACENT cells are exempt: the partially-filled
   180	    // surface band legitimately sits below rest density, and sucking on it pumps the surface.
   181	    // Neighbor air test reads .w ≥ 0.5: both CELL_AIR and a same-pass CELL_POCKET upgrade
   182	    // qualify, so the in-flight upgrade race cannot change the outcome (determinism).
   183	    if (cm.y > 0.0 && cm.w < 0.5) {
   184	        var near_air = false;
   185	        for (var a = 0; a < 3; a = a + 1) {
   186	            for (var s = -1; s <= 1; s = s + 2) {
   187	                var nb = cc;
   188	                nb[a] = nb[a] + s;
   189	                if (cell_in_range(nb) && cell_meta[cell_index(nb)].w >= 0.5) {
   190	                    near_air = true;
   191	                }
   192	            }
   193	        }
   194	        // params.dbg.x gates the suction on/off (production = on; the stirring isolation gate
   195	        // disables it). The deficit-driven suction is the original un-banded feedback — the
   196	        // settled-pool stirring fix is the G2P global PIC blend (PIC_BLEND_DEFAULT), shipped now
   197	        // that the crater gate asserts persistence (a held crater is correct, so the blend is safe).
   198	        // Under-density (−) suction half. Legacy (dbg.w ≤ 0.5): rate-limited by
   199	        // DENSITY_RELAX_FRAMES. Uncapped path (dbg.w > 0.5): the full predicted deficit at
   200	        // density-error dimension (rate e/dt), dead-banded by DENSITY_TARGET_DEADBAND — together
   201	        // with the cell_classify over-density half this forms one signed two-sided target, applied
   202	        // ONLY to interior fluid rows (the !near_air gate, KTD5). dbg.x = 0 still disables it.
   203	        // (Calibration: this suction fine-tunes the interior toward rest; the over-pack lever is
   204	        // the uncapped over-density half. Compliance was tried and dropped — it re-softened.)
   205	        let db = select(0.0, DENSITY_TARGET_DEADBAND, params.dbg.w > 0.5);
   206	        let deficit = min(cm.z / params.extra.x - 1.0 + db, 0.0);
   207	        if (params.dbg.x > 0.5 && !near_air && deficit < 0.0) {
   208	            // Temper-K rate divisor (dbg.z, default 0 ⇒ K=1 full uncap) — matches the cell_classify
   209	            // over-density half so the two-sided target shares one rate.
   210	            let kfac = max(params.dbg.z, 1.0);
   211	            var s_under: f32;
   212	            if (params.dbg.w > 0.5) {
   213	                s_under = deficit / (kfac * params.dt);
   214	            } else {
   215	                s_under = deficit / (DENSITY_RELAX_FRAMES * params.dt);
   216	            }
   217	            cell_meta[c].x = cm.x + cm.y * s_under / params.dt;
   218	        }
   219	        return;
   220	    }
   221	    if (cm.w != CELL_AIR || label > 0.5) {
   222	        return;
   223	    }
   224	    // Enclosed: compute the cell MIXTURE divergence (same φ-weighted corner gather as
   225	    // cell_classify — one family, U6).
   226	    let h = params.grid_origin.w;
   227	    var div = 0.0;
   228	    for (var oz = 0; oz < 2; oz = oz + 1) {
   229	        for (var oy = 0; oy < 2; oy = oy + 1) {
   230	            for (var ox = 0; ox < 2; ox = ox + 1) {
   231	                let s = corner_sign(vec3<i32>(ox, oy, oz));
   232	                let nflat = node_index(cc + vec3<i32>(ox, oy, oz));
   233	                let gv = grid_vel[nflat];
   234	                let phin = nm[2u * nflat + 1u].w;
   235	                div = div + dot(s, phin * gv.xyz) / (4.0 * h);
   236	            }
   237	        }
   238	    }
   239	    cell_meta[c] = vec4<f32>((0.0 - div) / params.dt, 1.0, 0.0, CELL_POCKET);
   240	    bubble[2] = 1.0; // an enclosed pocket exists: arm the bubble-row solves this frame
   241	    // Append this fine pocket cell to the compacted list (slot 0 is the count).
   242	    let slot = atomicAdd(&pocket_f[0], 1u);
   243	    atomicStore(&pocket_f[slot + 1u], c);
   244	}
   245	
   246	// =================================== bubble row relaxation =====================================
   247	// Shared single-workgroup reduction shape for both levels: each thread grid-strides the cell
   248	// range accumulating the pocket row sums (Σ rhs, Σ (A p̃)_c, Σ (A·1_pocket)_c), tree-reduce,
   249	// thread 0 solves the single-unknown row exactly. Runs BEFORE each Jacobi sweep, so the sweep
   250	// writes the fresh multiplier into the pocket slots (the Dirichlet copy).
   251	var<workgroup> red_rhs: array<f32, 256>;
   252	var<workgroup> red_ap: array<f32, 256>;
   253	var<workgroup> red_diag: array<f32, 256>;
   254	
   255	@compute @workgroup_size(256)
   256	fn bubble_fine(@builtin(local_invocation_id) lid: vec3<u32>) {
   257	    let t = lid.x;
   258	    // No open-cavity early-out here: a storage-buffer-gated `return` BEFORE a workgroupBarrier()
   259	    // is a Tint uniformity violation (Tint treats every read_write storage load as non-uniform,
   260	    // regardless of the value being equal across threads — native naga tolerates it, the browser
   261	    // rejects it and fails the whole module). The no-pocket case is already handled for free:
   262	    // when no pocket exists `pocket_f[0]` is 0, so `trips` is 0, the reduction sums zeros, and the
   263	    // thread-0 solve's `red_diag > 1e-12` guard yields λ_b = 0 — identical to the old early-out.
   264	    // U8 R9: stride the COMPACTED pocket list (a few hundred entries) not all ~76k fine cells.
   265	    // `count` is uniform across the workgroup (single atomic load, no in-flight append —
   266	    // pocket_mark finished last frame-pass), so the trip count stays uniform and every
   267	    // workgroupBarrier() below is reached from uniform control flow.
   268	    let count = atomicLoad(&pocket_f[0]);
   269	    let h = params.grid_origin.w;
   270	    var s_rhs = 0.0;
   271	    var s_ap = 0.0;
   272	    var s_diag = 0.0;
   273	    let trips = (count + 255u) / 256u; // uniform trip count (barrier discipline)
   274	    for (var it = 0u; it < trips; it = it + 1u) {
   275	        let li = it * 256u + t;
   276	        if (li < count) {
   277	            let c = atomicLoad(&pocket_f[li + 1u]);
   278	            let cc = vec3<i32>(cell_coords(c));
   279	            var acc_p = 0.0; // (D M̃⁻¹ G p̃)_c
   280	            var acc_i = 0.0; // (D M̃⁻¹ G 1_pocket)_c — aggregated diagonal incl. cross terms
   281	            for (var oz = 0; oz < 2; oz = oz + 1) {
   282	                for (var oy = 0; oy < 2; oy = oy + 1) {
   283	                    for (var ox = 0; ox < 2; ox = ox + 1) {
   284	                        let o = vec3<i32>(ox, oy, oz);
   285	                        let node = cc + o;
   286	                        let nidx = node_index(node);
   287	                        let m = Minv(nm[2u * nidx + 0u], nm[2u * nidx + 1u]);
   288	                        var gp = vec3<f32>(0.0);
   289	                        var gi = vec3<f32>(0.0);
   290	                        for (var qz = 0; qz < 2; qz = qz + 1) {
   291	                            for (var qy = 0; qy < 2; qy = qy + 1) {
   292	                                for (var qx = 0; qx < 2; qx = qx + 1) {
   293	                                    let c2 = node - vec3<i32>(1) + vec3<i32>(qx, qy, qz);
   294	                                    if (!cell_in_range(c2)) {
   295	                                        continue;
   296	                                    }
   297	                                    let ci2 = cell_index(c2);
   298	                                    let cm2 = cell_meta[ci2];
   299	                                    if (cm2.y <= 0.0) {
   300	                                        continue;
   301	                                    }
   302	                                    let s2 = corner_sign(vec3<i32>(1) - vec3<i32>(qx, qy, qz));
   303	                                    gp = gp - s2 * cm2.y * pf_src[ci2] / (4.0 * h);
   304	                                    if (cm2.w == CELL_POCKET) {
   305	                                        gi = gi - s2 * cm2.y / (4.0 * h);
   306	                                    }
   307	                                }
   308	                            }
   309	                        }
   310	                        let s = corner_sign(o);
   311	                        // φ_f node weight — same A = −D·Φ·M̃⁻¹·G family as the sweeps (U6).
   312	                        acc_p = acc_p + m.b.w * dot(s, minv_apply(m, gp)) / (4.0 * h);
   313	                        acc_i = acc_i + m.b.w * dot(s, minv_apply(m, gi)) / (4.0 * h);
   314	                    }
   315	                }
   316	            }
   317	            s_rhs = s_rhs + cell_meta[c].x;
   318	            s_ap = s_ap + (-acc_p); // row weight f = 1
   319	            s_diag = s_diag + (-acc_i);
   320	        }
   321	    }
   322	    red_rhs[t] = s_rhs;
   323	    red_ap[t] = s_ap;
   324	    red_diag[t] = s_diag;
   325	    workgroupBarrier();
   326	    var off = 128u;
   327	    loop {
   328	        if (t < off) {
   329	            red_rhs[t] = red_rhs[t] + red_rhs[t + off];
   330	            red_ap[t] = red_ap[t] + red_ap[t + off];
   331	            red_diag[t] = red_diag[t] + red_diag[t + off];
   332	        }
   333	        workgroupBarrier();
   334	        if (off == 1u) {
   335	            break;
   336	        }
   337	        off = off / 2u;
   338	    }
   339	    if (t == 0u) {
   340	        // Sub-resolution release (header: MIN_POCKET_FINE_CELLS): a pocket too small to be a
   341	        // resolved incompressible bubble is open air — λ = 0, present-flag cleared (so the next
   342	        // frame's bubble solves early-out and pocket_present() reads false). Guards the residual
   343	        // V60-cone draining-film entrainment without touching the large pour cavity.
   344	        if (count < MIN_POCKET_FINE_CELLS) {
   345	            bubble[0] = 0.0;
   346	            bubble[1] = 0.0;
   347	            bubble[2] = 0.0;
   348	            return;
   349	        }
   350	        // Fold the prolongated coarse correction into the scalar (exact for one scalar), then
   351	        // solve the aggregated row exactly given the current fluid pressure.
   352	        var lam = bubble[0] + bubble[1];
   353	        bubble[1] = 0.0;
   354	        if (red_diag[0] > 1.0e-12) {
   355	            lam = lam + (red_rhs[0] - red_ap[0]) / red_diag[0];
   356	        } else {
   357	            lam = 0.0; // no coupled pocket faces: the bubble is inactive (p = 0 air)
   358	        }
   359	        bubble[0] = lam;
   360	    }
   361	}
   362	
   363	// The identical step on the COARSE error equation: pocket-coarse cells (cmeta.w, set by
   364	// coarse_cell_setup: every active child a pocket cell — the rediscretization doctrine keeps
   365	// mixed boundary cells as fluid rows, smoothed at fine level) share the correction δλ_b.
   366	@compute @workgroup_size(256)
   367	fn bubble_coarse(@builtin(local_invocation_id) lid: vec3<u32>) {
   368	    let t = lid.x;
   369	    // No storage-gated early return before the barriers (Tint uniformity — see bubble_fine). The
   370	    // no-pocket case falls out for free: count 0 ⇒ trips 0 ⇒ zero reduction ⇒ δλ_b = 0.
   371	    // U8 R9: stride the COMPACTED coarse pocket list (see bubble_fine). `count` is uniform.
   372	    let count = atomicLoad(&pocket_c[0]);
   373	    let hc = params.grid_origin.w * f32(params.coarse_dims.w);
   374	    var s_rhs = 0.0;
   375	    var s_ap = 0.0;
   376	    var s_diag = 0.0;
   377	    let trips = (count + 255u) / 256u;
   378	    for (var it = 0u; it < trips; it = it + 1u) {
   379	        let li = it * 256u + t;
   380	        if (li < count) {
   381	            let c = atomicLoad(&pocket_c[li + 1u]);
   382	            let cc = vec3<i32>(ccell_coords(c));
