docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:63:- KTD-3 — **Darcy drag is a velocity body force folded semi-implicitly into the grid update — never a divergence penalty.** Form: drag rate β(φ) from `src/models/permeability.rs` (Kozeny–Carman), applied per node between the two velocity fields via the analytic exponential (Laibe–Price) update `Δv⁺ = Δv·exp(−β·dt)` — exact for frozen-coefficient linear drag at any stiffness (β refreshes per substep; when β varies in-step through φ, slip, or Re the update is formally first-order, so the honest claim is robust stability at coffee's worst-case density ratio ρ_f/ρ_s ≈ 0.83, not unconditional exactness), momentum-conserving by construction (mass-weighted pair update). Main's divergence-penalty formulation is recorded as a named anti-pattern: it blocks interface entry flux and is the root cause of the stuck water layer. This per-node analytic fold is the same structure production Euler-Euler codes use for stiff interphase drag (Fluent PC-SIMPLE's Partial Elimination Algorithm; MFiX-Exa reports drag iteration counts dropping from 50+ to 3–5 with it) — a 2×2 closed-form inversion, zero global communication. Two production refinements are adopted: (1) **drag-law blending** — Kozeny-Carman/Ergun is the packed-bed law and over-predicts drag in dilute regions (pour entry, splashed grains); blend toward a dilute-suspension law (Wen-Yu form) below φ_s ≈ 0.2 with a smooth transition (the Gidaspow/Huilin-Gidaspow pattern every TFM code ships); (2) if residual added-mass jitter appears despite the exponential fold, the standard stabilizer is a **virtual-mass term** (C_vm ≈ 0.5) added symmetrically to both phases — a named lever, default off.
docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:65:- KTD-5 — **Bed constitutive model: Klar et al. 2016 Drucker-Prager return map** (3-branch, log-strain, one 3×3 SVD per solid particle per substep) with saturation-dependent cohesion from `src/models/cohesion.rs` (Bishop-style effective stress) and a compaction cap surface for tamping memory (plastic volumetric strain persists and feeds packing fraction → permeability). The tensile-apex branch is what lets crater walls stand and then collapse. **Stress partition is stated once and audited:** total stress = effective stress (DP + cap, with the U5 over-packing solids-pressure guard living INSIDE the contact/effective partition) + pore pressure, and the projection pressure IS the pore pressure — no volumetric mode may be resisted twice by contact pressure, cap pressure, solids-pressure guard, and projection pressure stacking up. The U7 stress-partition audit gates this.
docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:140:- **Approach:** Quadratic B-spline weights (KEEP.md §3 validated math), fixed-point `atomic<i32>` P2G scatter with documented FP_SCALE/velocity-cap headroom, per-particle affine C matrix carried and updated in G2P. Gravity on the grid, plus grid-node solid-boundary treatment against the scene SDF solids (separating/no-penetration condition on grid velocities, mirroring `src/utils/sdf.rs` conventions with a "mirrors utils::sdf" WGSL comment) — boundary handling is scoped work here, not an afterthought. No pressure yet — this unit's water is a momentum-correct splashing dust.
docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:155:- **Test scenarios:** operator unit gates run BEFORE any fluid test (the production MMS/code-verification pattern, Salari-Knupp): discrete adjointness `u·(Gp) = −(Du)·p` to machine precision for random fields on the staggered layout, the same check for the coarse restriction/prolongation pair, a manufactured-solution order-of-accuracy sweep on D/G/L (observed log-log error slope matches the formal order), and — decisively — the same checks on the ASSEMBLED projection operator `A = −D·M⁻¹·G` exactly as used in the solve (mass/φ weighting, solid masks, boundary rows included), at both fine and coarse-with-transfer levels, on masked domains representative of real scenes (closed tank, sloped wall, V60 cone, partially filled bed) — a self-consistent D/G pair must not be able to pass while the seeded solve injects pressure through a different operator, and boundary-adjacent restriction/prolongation is exactly where multigrid-like schemes break, so box-only tests are insufficient; a two-grid convergence factor measured on known low- and high-frequency modes of those masked domains; then post-projection RMS divergence — measured with the projection's own divergence operator, interior cells only (surface cells are gated in U4) — drops by at least a stated factor (≥2×) per doubling of the fine-sweep budget until it falls below a pre-registered absolute tolerance, where the tolerance is derived from the visible-error budget (the xpbd density-band envelope) and the sweep count needed to reach it must fit the rung's pre-registered wall-clock ceiling (meeting tolerance only at non-real-time sweep counts fails L0 now, not L3 later); because the self-measured divergence gate is gameable, independent volume gates run alongside it: particle-density drift band, tank water-height drift, zero net flux through closed walls, free-surface fill-fraction conservation; a floor that plateaus above tolerance FAILS the gate (monotonic-but-plateauing was exactly main's A≠D·G signature); run on both a static tank and mid-splash dam break; A/B coarse-seed-on vs off shows the seed removes low-frequency residual (tank pressure profile approaches hydrostatic); with the adaptive-Tait predictor enabled, an A/B run must show a measurable fine-iteration-budget reduction at equal divergence tolerance — below threshold the predictor is removed rather than shipped dormant; density band on settled dam break matches the existing xpbd water-gate envelope; cost gate — dispatches/frame within the recorded U1 budget + a stated increment; long-run (≥2000 steps) settled tank stays settled (no pressure-driven creep or popcorn).
docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:176:- **Approach:** Per-solid-particle deformation gradient F (or elastic strain in log space), 3×3 SVD in WGSL (port a verified branch-free routine; CPU twin mandatory), Klar 3-branch return map (elastic / yield-surface projection / tensile apex), friction angle from `Materials`, cohesion from `src/models/cohesion.rs` as a function of local saturation (dry in this rung), volumetric cap surface whose consolidation pressure ratchets with plastic compaction → packing fraction state per particle. Grid-level over-packing guard (the TFM solids-pressure pattern): φ_s is hard-clipped at the packing limit and a solids-pressure term that diverges as φ_s → φ_max resists further compaction in the two-field update — the particle-level return map alone cannot guarantee this on the grid. The guard enters the solid momentum equation as part of the effective/contact stress per KTD-5's partition — it is NOT a separate volume constraint and never appears in the projection; the U7 stress-partition audit verifies it is counted exactly once. Cost bound: solid counts are ~10–15k grains against 100k+ water, so the SVD/return-map is bounded; demoting it from per-substep to per-frame is a permitted knob ONLY if the repose/collapse gates are shown insensitive to the choice.
docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:179:- **Test scenarios:** CPU-twin SVD matches a reference decomposition on random matrices including degenerate cases; return map satisfies yield-surface KKT conditions (stress inside surface after return, no spurious plastic flow in elastic regime); single-particle stress cycles show no energy gain; collapsed column forms a heap with repose angle ≥30° at coffee-like friction angle, and repose varies monotonically with friction angle (discrimination) while staying insensitive to grid resolution and wall friction within stated bands (confound control — the heap angle must track the material parameter, not numerics); heap at rest exhibits zero drift over 1200 frames (xpbd no-creep standard); repeated vertical press (tamp probe) increases packing fraction persistently across unload cycles — the plastic-memory gate that neither prior attempt had; a column pressed past the packing limit rejects further compaction (φ_s never exceeds φ_max anywhere — over-packing guard gate).
docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:291:- Fluent KTGF granular closures (Theory Guide §16.5): solids pressure with radial-distribution divergence at φ_max, Schaeffer/Johnson-Jackson frictional stress — the over-packing guard in U5.

